# TEMPLATE — copied to `allowed_ips` on first setup, then owned by the app.
#
# The live file is NOT tracked in git. This one is the more important of the
# pair to keep out: raw-IP entries are by definition somebody's specific
# infrastructure — a LAN MinIO, an internal warehouse — and committing them
# publishes a small map of the operator's network.
#
# Allowlisted egress IPs for notebook kernels (squid dst). dstdomain cannot
# match raw-IP URLs, so IP entries from
# notebook_runtime_settings.egress_allowlist are written here instead.
#
# Deliberately empty: a fresh install allows no raw IPs. Add them under
# Admin → Developer runtime, e.g. a LAN object store on 192.168.1.10:19000.
